WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.920
Low frequency sounds of
the sort that your voice is

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.600
that late night FM DJ
voice are responded to

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.080
in the brain by neurons,
no surprise there,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.410
but the frequency that those neurons fire

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.030
is also low frequency.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.530
In other words, when you
speak in your low voice.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.970
Right.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.790
The other person's brain hears that

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.030
and starts firing in a low frequency tone.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.430
In other words, it entrains to your voice,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.830
not just the timing, but it's actually

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.580
like you're essentially
playing an emotional piano down

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.620
in the low keys of their--

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.453
Oh, right.

00:00:41.453 --> 00:00:42.630
Of their mind.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.300
Now, when you go up to
the high frequencies,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.030
the neurons can't follow
that high frequency.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.450
So there's something special
about low frequency sound

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.750
that actually changes the emotional tone

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.303
of the people that hear
that low frequency sound.

